<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 9.99 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 9.99 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Thursday sold two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one week and four weeks, yielding 3.64 percent and 17.52 percent to maturity respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total of 11.541 billion levs of</p>
<p>T-bills but the ministry approved bids for 9.991 billion levs</p>
<p>worth.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG 3012097005     BG3012197003</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  January 23, 1997   January 23, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    January 23, 1997   January 23, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 January 30, 1997   February 20, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 6,751 million levs     4,790 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.48 pct	    85.05 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 6,531 million levs     3,460 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.49 pct	    85.09 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity	3.64 pct	    17.52 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
